{#
  Two tiny inline scripts that must run before the first paint, so they
  cannot live in the deferred bundle.

  1. Safety net for the reveal animation: sections only start invisible if
     JavaScript really runs. If js/main.js fails to load within two
     seconds, the `js` class is removed again and everything shows up.
     Without it half the page would be blank – and Google would see an
     empty page.
  2. PREVIEW ONLY (remove with the theme toggle before launch): applies a
     light/dark choice made with the toggle before rendering, otherwise
     the system scheme would flash briefly. The choice is saved by
     scripts/modules/theme-toggle.js.
#}
<script>
  document.documentElement.classList.add('js');
  setTimeout(function () {
    if (!window.__siteReady) document.documentElement.classList.remove('js');
  }, 2000);
</script>
<script>
  try {
    var t = localStorage.getItem('theme');
    if (t === 'light' || t === 'dark') document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', t);
  } catch (e) {}
</script>
